# pos_takeoff_climb_gust.scn — transmitter-ARM POS_HOLD auto-takeoff with a horizontal gust during the climb only: the craft returns toward the launch point
#                              上昇中だけ水平の突風を受ける送信機 ARM の POS_HOLD 自動離陸: 機体は発進点の方へ戻る
#
# The same disturbance as api_takeoff_climb_gust.scn (0.04 N behind the craft for 0.7 s, from just after the estimator releases its pin at 8.64 s to just before the climb completes at about 9.3 s)
# on the takeoff started by the transmitter ARM in POS_HOLD. That takeoff never re-captures its hold target at the completion, so it is the reference the API takeoff is brought to: it passes
# with and without the API fix (the two builds give the same numbers). At the completion the craft is 0.22 m from its launch point (truth); the estimate stays within -0.02 .. +0.06 m of the release
# point during the hold and the craft lands 0.08 m from the launch point. The hold is judged from 12 s to 20.4 s (before the DISARM that lands), the landing at 24 s.
# api_takeoff_climb_gust.scn と同じ外乱（機体の後ろ向き 0.04 N を 0.7 s、推定器が 8.64 s に固定を解いた直後から、上昇が完了する約 9.3 s の直前まで）を、POS_HOLD の送信機 ARM で始めた
# 自動離陸に加える。この離陸は完了のときに保持の目標を取り直さないので、API の `takeoff` を合わせる基準で、API の修正の有無によらず合格する（二つのビルドの数値は同じ）。完了のとき、機体は離陸点から
# 0.22 m（真値）にいて、保持の間、推定は解除の点から -0.02〜+0.06 m に収まり、機体は離陸点から 0.08 m の所に着陸する。保持は 12 s〜20.4 s（着陸の DISARM の前）、着陸は 24 s 以降に判定する。
# SILS has no flow-sensor error at low height, so this checks HOW the target is taken, not the size of the drift of a real flight. / SILS は低い高さのフローの誤差を持たないので、目標の取り方の確認であり、実機のずれの大きさの確認ではない。
#
# Run: sf sils scenario simulator/sils/scenarios/pos_takeoff_climb_gust.scn --target vehicle --duration 28000000
#
#  <t>  ch    <thr> <roll> <pitch> <yaw> <arm> <hold_ms> <rate_hz> <alt> <acro> <pos>
   0    rc    2048  2048   2048    2048  0     6000      50                       # A: boot at rest — calibration completes (t=0-6)
   +    rc    2048  2048   2048    2048  0     1500      50        0     0     1  # B: POS switch ON while DISARMED (t=6-7.5)
   +    rc    2048  2048   2048    2048  1     1150      50        0     0     1  # C: ARM in POS_HOLD -> auto-takeoff; the estimator releases its pin at 8.64 s (t=7.5-8.65)
   +    wind  0.0 -0.04 0.0                                                        # D: gust ON: 0.04 N behind the craft (true -East), the climb only
   +    rc    2048  2048   2048    2048  1     700       50        0     0     1  # E: climb under the gust (t=8.65-9.35); the takeoff completes at about 9.4 s
   +    wind  0.0 0.0 0.0                                                          # F: gust OFF
   +    rc    2048  2048   2048    2048  1     11050     50        0     0     1  # G: the hold (t=9.35-20.4)
   +    rc    2048  2048   2048    2048  0     200       50                       # H: release ARM button
   +    rc    2048  2048   2048    2048  1     200       50                       # I: press again -> DISARM -> autonomous landing in POS_HOLD (t=20.6)
   +    rc    2048  2048   2048    2048  0     6000      50                       # J: touchdown and rest (t=20.8-26.8)
